# MITTA — provider API keys, for development.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   chmod 600 .env
#   # then paste your keys below
#
# `.env` is gitignored (`.env` and `.env.*` are covered, with `.env.example`
# explicitly re-included). Nothing you put there is committed. Verify it
# yourself before pasting anything — do not take this comment's word for it:
#
#   git check-ignore -v .env
#
# In the shipped application these keys live in the macOS Keychain instead,
# entered through Settings so they never touch a file at all (R3, DEC-017). This
# file is the development path: it survives a sidecar restart without a UI
# round-trip, which matters when you are iterating on provider code.
#
# Rotate anything that has ever been pasted into a chat window, a terminal that
# logs history, or a screenshot. Treat those keys as public.

# Primary provider. https://console.groq.com/keys
MITTA_GROQ_API_KEY=

# Secondary provider, used when Groq is rate-limited or down.
# https://openrouter.ai/keys
MITTA_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
